# TurnKey CRM

You are working on TurnKey, a CRM with React + Vite frontend, Supabase backend, and Netlify deployment.

## Architecture

- Frontend talks directly to Supabase via `@supabase/supabase-js`
- Database schema lives in `supabase/migrations/`
- Types are in `src/lib/database.types.ts` (regenerate with `npm run db:types`)
- Netlify serves the Vite SPA from `dist/` with SPA redirects in `netlify.toml`

## Code style

- TypeScript strict mode
- Use `@/` imports
- Keep pages in `src/pages/`, shared UI in `src/components/`
- Minimal scope changes — match existing patterns

## Supabase rules

- Every new table needs RLS enabled and explicit policies
- Never expose service role keys to the frontend
- Migrations are the source of truth for schema

## Multi-tool workflow

This repo is shared across Cursor, Claude Code, and ChatGPT. Before large changes, check `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` for the agreed workflow. Update `CLAUDE.md` when architecture changes.
